WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.430
<b>Necessary Evil</b>

3
00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:58.820
Well?

4
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.560
You like my star shield?

5
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.930
What's up with this guy's body?

6
00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.800
There's no way a human
could do this stuff!

7
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.740
Spitting fire again?!

8
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.710
Master Nails!

9
00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.740
Moon Walk!

10
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.620
Hey, stop jumping around!

11
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.880
We're getting nowhere!

12
00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.480
I was hoping my Four
Powers would be enough,

13
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.580
but I guess not.

14
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.520
I'm afraid I haven't mastered
the Finger Pistol yet.

15
00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.990
But I've got a little stand-in

16
00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.330
that should do the
job quite nicely.

17
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.260
All right!

18
00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.030
This is my chance to go to the next car!

19
00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.400
Hey, I thought we were
having a fight, here!

20
00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.030
He thinks he's smart.

21
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.180
I got you now.

22
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.020
Beans Left!

23
00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.580
Nice try.

24
00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.860
But I saw that coming
from a mile away!

25
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.600
That hurt!

26
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.500
I get it.

27
00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.680
You son of a bitch,
Ouchie Finger!

28
00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.880
Shave!

29
00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.920
This ain't good.

30
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.680
He's got my number now.

31
00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.220
Tempest Kick!

32
00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.010
Just grazed me!

33
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.760
He sure moves
around a lot, though.

34
00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.680
I know your weak point!

35
00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.520
It's your back, isn't it?

36
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.400
And that's not
counting your brain,

37
00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.510
which is an obvious
weakness, too.

38
00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.680
At this rate, it's only a matter of time
before you're finished.

39
00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.580
Don't get ahead of yourself, pal.

40
00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.590
I got a move that'll get
rid of my weak point easy!

41
00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.720
Franky Invincible!

42
00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.860
Eat that!

43
00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.750
<b>Invincible</b>

44
00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.920
Now do you give
up, weasel face?!

45
00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.550
That's so stupid, I don't even have a
comeback.

46
00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.850
Anyway, this is nothing but bad luck.

47
00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.540
Well, bad luck for you, I mean.

48
00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.940
Did I mention I was super this week?

49
00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.220
It's not a good time to make me angry.

50
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.460
Let me ask you something, brother.

51
00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.690
Have you ever heard of the
creature they call a "Centaur"?

52
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.330
Hm?

53
00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.030
You mean those
things that are human

54
00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.470
from the waist up and like
a horse from the waist down?

55
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.360
Yeah, what about them?

56
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.440
Convert!

57
00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.160
<b>Convert</b>

58
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.910
<b>Pervert</b>

59
00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.230
No way.

60
00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:46.630
That's ridiculous!

61
00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:50.700
Franky... Centaur Mode!

62
00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:51.900
It's backwards!

63
00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.080
Your head's supposed to be in the front,
not your crotch!

64
00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.690
You call this backwards?

65
00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:02.180
Just wait 'til I rearrange
your face, weasel boy.

66
00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.200
Damn it you crook cook!
Don't talk saucy to me!

67
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.670
My awesome noodle fists are all gone!

68
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:07.800
What am I?

69
00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.340
An onion?!

70
00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.410
If you're an onion,

71
00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.680
you're gonna make yourself
cry if you keep this up.

72
00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.680
Just quit while you're ahead.

73
00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.780
I won't cry and I won't quit!

74
00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.280
Who said I was gonna lose?!

75
00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.170
After all, I'm Wanze, CP7's ace!

76
00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.810
I may look like I'm having fun,

77
00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.210
but I take this
mission very seriously.

78
00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.040
The government's been
chasing Robin for years

79
00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.910
and I'm not gonna
be the one to blow it

80
00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.610
now that we finally have her!

81
00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:35.750
So maybe you're the one

82
00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.650
who should quit
while you're ahead!

83
00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.810
Now Ramen Kenpo!

84
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.980
Noodle Nail Knockout!

85
00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:49.950
When cutting an onion,

86
00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.120
you need to sever the stem

87
00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.850
and the root without
harming the flesh.

88
00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.120
If you chop through the
fiber with one clean stroke

89
00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.760
the surface will
retain its glossy shine.

90
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.000
Stop it!

91
00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:05.830
Go away!

92
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.850
Ramen Beam!

93
00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.770
Epluchage!

94
00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.780
You... You cut me!

95
00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.750
Huh? You didn't cut me?

96
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.650
Sure peeling onions
may not be glamorous,

97
00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.390
but you have to put love into
every aspect of your cooking.

98
00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.690
Kitchen knives aren't for cutting people.

99
00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.820
You don't treat them like swords.

100
00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.000
However, they did a fine job of cutting
down that armor.

101
00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.830
Kitchen Knife Throw!

102
00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.800
Punk!

103
00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.070
Œil!

104
00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.030
My eyes! They're caving in!

105
00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.240
Let 'em.

106
00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:08.380
Now, shut your
mouth and give up.

107
00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.020
Yeah, you wish!

108
00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:14.690
I don't get it.

109
00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.220
Why do you want to
save that terrible woman

110
00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.200
so much in the first place?!

111
00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:21.300
Or maybe Nico Robin's
got you all fooled.

112
00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.500
You want me to tell
you the truth, huh?

113
00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.530
Think you can take it?

114
00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:26.400
Nez!

115
00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:27.270
Joue!

116
00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.350
Bouche!

117
00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.680
Dents!

118
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.580
Menton!

119
00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.660
If you keep talking like that,

120
00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:38.160
I'm gonna re-arrange your face.

121
00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:40.860
Hold on a sec.

122
00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.800
Anything but the face!

123
00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.530
Cut it out!

124
00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.410
Everyone knows she's bad news.

125
00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:50.820
It's no secret!

126
00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:51.600
She's evil!

127
00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.340
A monster!

128
00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.870
Better off dead!

129
00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.420
Parage Shot!

130
00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.400
Damn it, I think
my face caved in!

131
00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.330
I need a mirror.

132
00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:31.460
How could you?!

133
00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.560
You fiend!

134
00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:36.360
You ruined my beautiful eyes
and my fabulous teeth!

135
00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:40.760
You're the devil, aren't you?!

136
00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.760
Hey, your face went back!

137
00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.430
You're right!

138
00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:46.130
Look!

139
00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.230
My inner beauty is shining!

140
00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.470
It was but a fleeting illusion.

141
00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.370
You're guilty of three sins.

142
00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:56.140
Let me list them.

143
00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.980
First off, you dared to call
yourself a chef in front of me.

144
00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.950
Second, you were
disrespectful to your food.

145
00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.880
And third, you insulted my friend.

146
00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.990
For that, you'll pay.

147
00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.400
Hiss!

148
00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:23.730
You put on a big show, but you're all bark
and no bite!

149
00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.200
Whether you've got
two legs or four,

150
00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:31.150
you still seem pretty
useless to me, centaur.

151
00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.430
Ah! No!

152
00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.170
Lookin' pretty pathetic, buddy.

153
00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.170
Shut up!

154
00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.400
Shall I give you a hand?

155
00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.140
No, no, no!

156
00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:01.410
Don't you dare!

157
00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.080
Just kidding!

158
00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.550
Give me a hand?

159
00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.020
You oughta be
ashamed of yourself,

160
00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:26.590
using a line like that!

161
00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:29.620
And what was that about
four legs being useless?

162
00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:31.590
I just needed to catch you!

163
00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.930
You can't run now!

164
00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.000
I hate you, you jerk!

165
00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.760
I just want to be me!

166
00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.750
Give me my individuality back!

167
00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.880
Right on the other side
of that door behind you,

168
00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:45.490
my friend is waiting
to be rescued.

169
00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.630
When I say no, I mean no!

170
00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:57.390
Ramen Kenpo Secret
Move Poison Pasta Cutter!

171
00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.970
Touch it and die!

172
00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.260
Go, go, go, go, go!

173
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.830
You people are pathetic!

174
00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.780
Nico Robin has you eating right out of her
hand!

175
00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.890
She's betrayed every
person she's ever met,

176
00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:09.990
and you're here risking
your life to save her?

177
00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.390
You're beyond help!

178
00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.920
It's time to die!

179
00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:20.700
Three-Spot Decoupage.

180
00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.920
Hiss! I didn't think
you'd use such a dumb trick!

181
00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.430
I let my guard down!

182
00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.830
Right!

183
00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.930
Oh, yeah, cause I'm
the dumb one here.

184
00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.870
Instead of making excuses
why don't you tell me

185
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:27.940
what you want written on
your gravestone, brother.

186
00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.910
Oh, I get it.

187
00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:33.580
You don't think this fight is over yet,
do you?

188
00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.220
What?

189
00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.590
Since you dodged all
my punches so far,

190
00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:40.030
I can't really blame you.

191
00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.930
You have no clue
how hard I can hit.

192
00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.470
It's gonna be a nasty surprise!

193
00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:55.810
Here's my Ultimate Hammer!

194
00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.850
Wow, some entrance.

195
00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.490
What the hell have you been doing?

196
00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.720
Ow!

197
00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.660
Well as per usual, I've been
kicking ass and what about you?

198
00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.860
Been kicking ass.

199
00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.650
It's gotten so noisy all of a sudden.

200
00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.080
I take it all of the escorts

201
00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.320
for this mission have
been annihilated then?

202
00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.420
Well, we weren't expecting much

203
00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:55.190
from them to begin with.

204
00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:58.190
So it's you, huh?

205
00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.460
You're the bastards who kidnapped Robin.

206
00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:01.660
Be careful.

207
00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.700
They use some
pretty weird moves.

208
00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.660
And who is this?

209
00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:11.320
Based on what Corgy said,

210
00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.690
he's probably that
new recruit for CP9.

211
00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.990
Name's Nero, he's
gone through training,

212
00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.560
knows four of the powers.

213
00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:22.670
Dammit!

214
00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.940
You're in for it now, you bastard!

215
00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.510
Nobody does that to me and gets away with
it!

216
00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.740
I'll show you why they call me the genius
of fighting!

217
00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.670
Now prepare to die!

218
00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.380
– Huh?
– Huh?

219
00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.700
Hey new guy.

220
00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.290
Let me guess,
you must be Rob Lucci.

221
00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.720
Sorry I didn't introduce myself.

222
00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:46.420
Just give me a moment and I'll kill this
troublemaker.

223
00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.780
Our orders were to bring him in alive.

224
00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:52.410
You've let your emotions get the better of
you, it seems.

225
00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.860
Well, that just won't do.

226
00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:59.170
I'll give you three seconds to run for
your life.

227
00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:00.840
Three.

228
00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.240
Run for my life?!

229
00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:03.240
Run from who?

230
00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:04.510
Two.

231
00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:05.490
What?!

232
00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.800
Stop kidding around, okay?!

233
00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.440
It's not funny!

234
00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.210
And one.

235
00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.380
No! Don't do it!

236
00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:32.880
You're nothing more than an incompetent
piece of trash.

237
00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.920
You call yourself CP9?

238
00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.080
Don't make me laugh.

239
00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:45.740
You have to master all Six
Powers to be one of us, rookie.

240
00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:46.410
Kalifa.

241
00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.570
Yes?

242
00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:51.840
On our official report, state:
"The new guy was too weak.

243
00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.050
He was therefore
deemed worthless."

244
00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.920
Understood.

245
00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:00.230
And these are the
agents of justice?

246
00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.740
Can't tell which
side is evil, huh?

247
00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.110
I suppose there's no need to ask

248
00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:10.710
what you're doing on
this train, intruder.

249
00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.310
Judging by the way
you opened the door,

250
00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.610
I know exactly the kind

251
00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.620
of impatient people
we're dealing with.

252
00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:17.550
Yeah.

253
00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.020
Guess you'll have to excuse my manners.

254
00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:22.960
You've come to rescue Nico Robin?

255
00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:24.570
That is a mistake.

256
00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:25.670
Listen.

257
00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:28.440
Her problem is one that's
beyond your comprehension.

258
00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:30.970
You see, there are
some people in this world

259
00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.380
who were just born
under a bad sign.

260
00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:37.980
People who are, for the sake of everyone
else, better off dead.

261
00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.990
For example.

262
00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.900
Suppose there exists
a sleeping devil.

263
00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:49.170
One that's capable of burning the entire
world to the ground.

264
00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.670
And what if there was someone

265
00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:52.410
with the ability
to wake that devil?

266
00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:57.250
Even if this someone happened to be an
eight-year-old girl.

267
00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.670
Don't you think
that for the lives

268
00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.820
of every other living
being on this planet,

269
00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.650
that girl should be put to death?

270
00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:06.490
Stop rambling and get to the point.

271
00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:09.800
What I just told you is the true story of
Nico Robin.

272
00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.630
Her very first transgression.

273
00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:15.280
And now, she's accumulated
an entire life of crime.

274
00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:16.980
As far back as she can remember,

275
00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:20.290
her very existence has
been nothing but a sin.

276
00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.710
The only good she can
do this world would be

277
00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:25.480
to forfeit her life
and disappear forever.

278
00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.820
That's the misfortune she carries with
her.

279
00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:28.920
She's cursed.

280
00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:33.150
She has no choice but to accept her fate
and die.

281
00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.850
Honestly, she should've
died over twenty years ago.

282
00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:39.690
We're merely correcting a wrong from the
past.

283
00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.530
It'll be better
for everyone else

284
00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:45.160
when this is over
and she's dead.

285
00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:46.660
Hey.

286
00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.510
That's enough!

287
00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.370
Bastard!

288
00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:56.210
I don't wanna hear
another word out of you!

289
00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:56.960
Pity.

290
00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.070
Her death won't come nearly as quickly as
I would like.

291
00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:05.940
Interrogations.

292
00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:06.810
Torture.

293
00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:07.780
Slowly.

294
00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.010
Repeatedly.

295
00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.650
The World Government is going
to keep her alive for years,

296
00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:13.680
squeezing out all
of her knowledge,

297
00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.750
experiences,
and intelligence.

298
00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:16.910
She'll know agony
before she dies.

299
00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.920
I'm not gonna let that happen!

300
00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:20.020
Wait! Robin! Please!

301
00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.860
Don't go in there!
No! Seriously!

302
00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:26.900
That's a really, really,
really bad idea! Stop!

303
00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:30.230
I said "Wait!"
not "Keep going!"

304
00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:31.140
Robin!

305
00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:32.780
There you are!

306
00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.020
We're in deep trouble.

307
00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:35.050
I'm so happy!

308
00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:35.990
Are you okay?

309
00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:36.990
Say something!

310
00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:38.890
Why are you doing this?!

311
00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:41.290
I went through all that trouble to sneak
in from the outside!

312
00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:43.930
I even took out that snoopy government
guy!

313
00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.330
So that's Nico Robin, huh?

314
00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.530
I'd buy that.

315
00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:53.370
Looks like the girl in the
wanted poster, that's for sure.

316
00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.760
Lemme knock these guys
out then we'll escape!

317
00:18:56.790 --> 00:19:01.030
We'll run away together and
leave all this behind us! 'Kay?

318
00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.990
It's gonna be all right!

319
00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:10.550
Usopp!

320
00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:13.770
Robin! What are you doing?!

321
00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:27.980
It seems that my words mean nothing to you
people.

322
00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:37.790
Franky! Quick!

323
00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.330
Detach the third car!

324
00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.830
Why? What are we gonna do?

325
00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:44.150
Run.

326
00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:44.980
We're gonna run?!

327
00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:46.680
What the heck are you talking about?

328
00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.020
You too, Sanji!

329
00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:48.750
Get ready!

330
00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.820
This will be over in a flash!

331
00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:52.690
Make sure that Franky doesn't escape!

332
00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.130
Right.

333
00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:03.100
Sniper King Smoke Star!

334
00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:10.470
What kind of a
stupid stunt is that?!

335
00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:14.770
Come on!

336
00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:15.710
I've got her!

337
00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.440
Move it!

338
00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:20.450
Put me down!

339
00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:23.820
Let go!

340
00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:28.020
– All right!
– All right!

341
00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:30.160
Whoa!

342
00:20:34.390 --> 00:20:41.890
Turn back!

343
00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.650
But we've already come so far!

344
00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:44.920
Answer us!

345
00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.350
– Yeah, tell us why!
– Yeah, tell us why!

346
00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.220
You better give us a reason!

347
00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:51.320
That's not what I meant!

348
00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.980
I was telling that
giant frog that jumped

349
00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.050
on the railway to turn back!

350
00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:58.860
He came out of nowhere!

351
00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.210
Gero! Gero! Gero!

352
00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:01.780
It's Yokozuna!

353
00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:03.210
Yokozuna?

354
00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:03.790
– No way!
– No way!

355
00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:04.690
Look out!

356
00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:06.490
A giant frog's on the tracks!

357
00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:08.210
Froggy!

358
00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:09.280
Turn back!

359
00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:10.620
Get out of the way!

360
00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.720
Gero!

361
00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:12.740
Look out!

362
00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:16.900
Yes!

363
00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.670
We did it!

364
00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.030
We got Robin back!

365
00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:25.970
You know I should be happy.

366
00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:29.040
But I'm not really a big fan
of this "running away" stuff.

367
00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.800
That smoke screen
was such a stupid idea

368
00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:34.360
that it actually surprised them.

369
00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:35.980
Whew!

370
00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:38.450
Sniper King says,
"The plan that involves us

371
00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:41.860
not fighting scary guys like
them is the best plan of all."

372
00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.630
Doubtful.

373
00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:46.510
Besides, that was too easy.

374
00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:47.540
Yeah.

375
00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:49.120
These guys aren't like the others.

376
00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.250
We shouldn't let our guard down just yet.

377
00:21:55.990 --> 00:21:57.520
What's that?

378
00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.760
Those thorny whips again?

379
00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:06.490
I've got them.

380
00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:07.590
Now, Blueno.

381
00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:08.720
Right.

382
00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:11.940
Quick! Cut those things!

383
00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:19.970
They're pulling us back!

384
00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:23.850
Whoa, these guys are powerful!

385
00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:30.290
Did you actually think a smoke screen
would stop us?

386
00:22:31.060 --> 00:22:34.070
Like I said, that was way too easy.

387
00:22:38.130 --> 00:22:41.540
Now remember, don't kill any of the Straw
Hats.

388
00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:44.010
That was our agreement.

389
00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:45.140
Hey, Sniper King.

390
00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:45.840
Yeah?

391
00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:47.220
Protect Robin with your life!

392
00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:48.320
Got it?

393
00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:48.800
What?

394
00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:49.700
Right!

395
00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:54.840
I'm gonna have to ask you to let our car
go!

396
00:22:57.970 --> 00:22:59.210
What the hell?

397
00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:00.910
His body's like a rock!

398
00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:04.400
I told you, these guys
use some weird moves!

399
00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:13.580
Concassé!

400
00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:24.920
Now that was a pretty powerful kick.

401
00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.160
It almost broke
through the Iron Body.

402
00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:28.130
Careful, Blueno.

403
00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:29.460
Don't take him lightly.

404
00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:31.160
He doesn't have a bounty on him,

405
00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:33.400
but he's one of
their main fighters.

406
00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:35.650
Whoa! Robin!
Hold on a sec!

407
00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:38.270
Wait! What are you doing?!

408
00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:40.110
Now Ocho Fleurs!

409
00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:41.650
With a Clutch!

410
00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:43.990
Long nose! Look out!

411
00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:50.160
Hey! Robin, what are you doing?!

412
00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:54.330
Didn't you hear me?

413
00:23:54.430 --> 00:23:55.500
Stay out of my business!

414
00:23:55.550 --> 00:23:56.880
Leave me alone!

415
00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:03.430
It can't be.

416
00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:06.470
Hey! Buddy! You
should learn to pay attention.

417
00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:15.060
Eyebrows!

418
00:24:18.460 --> 00:24:19.760
You Straw Hats are nuts!

419
00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:21.370
None of you make any damn sense!

420
00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:22.500
All of you are so stubborn,

421
00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:25.540
especially when it has anything
to do with your friends!

422
00:24:25.570 --> 00:24:27.410
Well, we've come this far.

423
00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:29.540
So, you want to escape, huh?

424
00:24:29.570 --> 00:24:34.240
Then here's your big chance!

425
00:25:01.080 --> 00:25:02.380
Franky!

426
00:25:16.430 --> 00:25:19.100
That was uncalled for.

427
00:25:19.130 --> 00:25:22.530
Didn't expect that, did ya?

428
00:25:22.570 --> 00:25:24.470
I don't understand your intentions.

429
00:25:24.500 --> 00:25:26.940
Why side with them in the first place?

430
00:25:26.970 --> 00:25:28.640
I couldn't take it anymore.

431
00:25:28.730 --> 00:25:29.830
No matter what she said or did,

432
00:25:29.890 --> 00:25:33.260
those two idiots weren't
gonna leave here without her.

433
00:25:33.320 --> 00:25:36.150
That still doesn't explain why you're
butting in on this.

434
00:25:36.150 --> 00:25:36.720
Ow!

435
00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:38.190
Hey, listen!

436
00:25:38.190 --> 00:25:38.820
Get outta here!

437
00:25:38.820 --> 00:25:40.060
Don't worry about me!

438
00:25:40.090 --> 00:25:41.260
I've got a plan!

439
00:25:41.290 --> 00:25:42.220
When you meet up with Straw Hat,

440
00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:45.490
find some way to get
back to Water Seven, okay?!

441
00:25:45.530 --> 00:25:46.300
Franky!

442
00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:47.200
Hold on!

443
00:25:47.230 --> 00:25:48.330
I'm not trying to escape!

444
00:25:48.330 --> 00:25:49.490
I won't run!

445
00:25:50.180 --> 00:25:52.650
Robin, what's wrong with you?

446
00:25:52.680 --> 00:25:53.680
Cut it out!

447
00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:55.790
There's no point in
trying to pretend anymore!

448
00:25:55.820 --> 00:25:57.450
We know, okay?

449
00:25:57.490 --> 00:26:02.090
We know what you did and
we came here to rescue you!

450
00:26:02.150 --> 00:26:03.080
It doesn't matter if they

451
00:26:03.090 --> 00:26:05.260
"Buster Call" us to
the ends of the world,

452
00:26:05.290 --> 00:26:06.660
we'll fight them and win!

453
00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:08.690
There's no reason for
you to keep obeying them

454
00:26:08.720 --> 00:26:11.060
and throw your life away!

455
00:26:16.570 --> 00:26:17.600
You're wrong.

456
00:26:17.630 --> 00:26:19.800
If there's a Buster Call.

457
00:26:25.210 --> 00:26:27.480
You'll be obliterated.

458
00:26:30.380 --> 00:26:36.480
Tempest Kick!

459
00:26:36.520 --> 00:26:38.050
Sanji!

460
00:26:44.620 --> 00:26:46.190
What just happened?

461
00:26:46.230 --> 00:26:47.660
He came outta nowhere.

462
00:26:47.690 --> 00:26:50.430
How did he do that?

463
00:26:53.420 --> 00:26:54.120
Huh?

464
00:26:54.120 --> 00:26:55.550
Blueno disappeared?

465
00:26:55.580 --> 00:26:57.590
Nothing of the sort.

466
00:26:57.620 --> 00:26:59.890
That's the power of
his Door-Door Fruit.

467
00:26:59.920 --> 00:27:02.360
He can create a
door out of thin air

468
00:27:02.390 --> 00:27:05.430
then use it to travel
to another location.

469
00:27:06.700 --> 00:27:09.700
At any rate, don't bother trying to
escape.

470
00:27:09.740 --> 00:27:11.970
It's simply not possible.

471
00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:28.420
Let Robin go.

472
00:27:31.890 --> 00:27:33.720
Finger Pistol.

473
00:27:40.890 --> 00:27:41.760
Usopp!

474
00:27:42.030 --> 00:27:43.940
Iron Body.

475
00:27:45.790 --> 00:27:47.960
Your last kick was a lot stronger.

476
00:27:48.070 --> 00:27:49.940
Tired already?

477
00:28:04.940 --> 00:28:06.780
Stubborn one, aren't you?

478
00:28:06.790 --> 00:28:08.960
Stop it!

479
00:28:08.990 --> 00:28:12.700
I promise, I have no intention of running
away.

480
00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:15.620
I'll honor the deal-you
don't have to hurt them.

481
00:28:15.620 --> 00:28:18.490
They're the ones who keep attacking me.

482
00:28:18.500 --> 00:28:20.440
What do you expect?

483
00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:23.840
Then let's hurry and leave before they get
up again.

484
00:28:26.940 --> 00:28:28.390
Wait!

485
00:28:33.970 --> 00:28:35.670
It's all right, Robin.

486
00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:38.340
We'll be fine.

487
00:28:38.370 --> 00:28:40.840
I understand what's going on.

488
00:28:41.120 --> 00:28:45.330
You're still hiding something from us,
aren't you?

489
00:28:48.310 --> 00:28:50.310
But there's one last thing.

490
00:28:52.430 --> 00:28:55.300
You can do what you want.

491
00:28:56.710 --> 00:29:02.400
But a pirate isn't
allowed to leave their crew.

492
00:29:02.400 --> 00:29:06.810
Unless they have their
captain's permission.

493
00:29:08.810 --> 00:29:11.380
So no matter what.

494
00:29:11.410 --> 00:29:16.620
You can always believe in Luffy.

495
00:29:35.190 --> 00:29:37.120
Robin, don't go!

496
00:29:37.160 --> 00:29:38.430
You can say what
you like to her,

497
00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:40.700
but she won't
break our agreement.

498
00:29:40.730 --> 00:29:42.960
How do you know that?

499
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:47.040
Long ago an island was erased.

500
00:29:47.970 --> 00:29:51.140
That is to say, the
Navy issued a Buster Call

501
00:29:51.170 --> 00:29:52.910
and burned it to the ground

502
00:29:52.940 --> 00:29:55.980
without leaving a
single trace behind.

503
00:29:56.070 --> 00:29:57.810
The only survivor
of that incident

504
00:29:57.810 --> 00:30:01.420
was Nico Robin,
still a child at the time.

505
00:30:01.450 --> 00:30:03.290
She never told us.

506
00:30:03.320 --> 00:30:06.120
Five vice admirals
and ten battleships

507
00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:08.890
are a terrifying force
for anyone to behold.

508
00:30:08.930 --> 00:30:12.100
But for a child to see
them destroy her home.

509
00:30:12.130 --> 00:30:15.400
Well, it's nothing short of a nightmare.

510
00:30:15.420 --> 00:30:18.290
Those thoughts have
haunted her for years

511
00:30:18.310 --> 00:30:20.910
and now that her old
nightmare bares its fangs

512
00:30:21.340 --> 00:30:24.890
at her companions she no longer
has the will to resist us.

513
00:30:25.050 --> 00:30:30.990
You bastards,
you knew and you used that.

514
00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:37.100
Of course we did.

515
00:30:37.130 --> 00:30:39.260
This is sick.

516
00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:42.670
You people are sick,
you hear me?!

517
00:30:42.670 --> 00:30:45.340
All of this is for the sake of justice.

518
00:30:45.370 --> 00:30:49.740
I sympathize with her, but I cannot be
swayed.

519
00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:51.910
Don't give me that crap!

520
00:31:10.660 --> 00:31:14.240
This isn't over!

521
00:31:16.870 --> 00:31:19.670
Enies Lobby Department
of Management here.

522
00:31:19.710 --> 00:31:21.980
Is everything in order regarding the
transfer?

523
00:31:22.010 --> 00:31:23.110
Yes.

524
00:31:23.140 --> 00:31:26.650
We will be delivering the two criminals on
schedule.

525
00:31:27.320 --> 00:31:30.690
We can see the island now, so expect us
soon.

526
00:31:30.720 --> 00:31:31.560
Understood.

527
00:31:31.790 --> 00:31:34.410
We'll make preparations for your return.

528
00:31:35.730 --> 00:31:37.830
I can't help but
feel a bit nostalgic

529
00:31:37.870 --> 00:31:40.540
after five years of absence.

530
00:31:40.570 --> 00:31:42.870
The Nightless Island, Enies Lobby.
